/-!
# Odd-weight dimension lower bound for M_k(Γ₁(M))

Theorem statement: `ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card_of_odd`
(`502ed595-0a14-5d67-a40a-29590288ac71`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `32af4b01-b7fd-5b8e-81f4-0fc04c36576c`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $M$ be a positive natural number with $M \ge 5$, and let $k$ be a natural number with $k \ge 3$
and $k$ odd. Then there exist a natural number $d$ and a family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to$
`ModularForm (Gamma1 M) (k : ℤ)` of modular forms of weight $k$ (the integer cast of $k$) for the
congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, linearly independent over
$\mathbb{C}$, such that
$$(k-1)\,\bigl[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M)\vee\langle -1\rangle\bigr] \; + \;
6\,\#\bigl(\Gamma_1(M) \backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) / \langle T, -1\rangle\bigr) \; \le \;
12\,d,$$
where the first index is that of the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by
$\Gamma_1(M)$ together with the integer powers of $-1$, i.e. of $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$; the subtraction
$k-1$ is in $\mathbb{N}$; and the second term counts the double cosets of $\Gamma_1(M)$ and of the
subgroup generated by the translation matrix `ModularGroup.T` and $-1$, a finite cardinality taken
via `Nat.card`. Thus the space of weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$ contains at least
$\bigl((k-1)[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_1(M)] + 6\,\#\text{cusps}\bigr)/12$ linearly
independent elements.

This is the odd-weight case of the lower bound on $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ coming from
the classical dimension formula, expressed as the existence of a linearly independent family rather
than as an equality of dimensions; the double-coset count is the number of cusps of $X_1(M)$ and the
index term is $[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_1(M)]$, which by the genus formula for $X_1(M)$
rewrites the bound as $\dim M_k \ge (k-1)(g-1) + kc/2$. Together with the even-weight case it feeds
[`ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card`]
(thm.html#ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card),
the uniform dimension lower bound used to produce modular forms of prescribed weight and level.

